[TITLE]
CRASH-12 scenario A: STEADY routing with one pollutant. The outfall is
listed before the junctions, so J2 (upstream node of C2) has node index 2
while there are only 2 links (indices 0 and 1). 1 cfs at 10 mg/L enters J1.

[OPTIONS]
FLOW_UNITS           CFS
INFILTRATION         HORTON
FLOW_ROUTING         STEADY
START_DATE           01/01/2020
START_TIME           00:00:00
REPORT_START_DATE    01/01/2020
REPORT_START_TIME    00:00:00
END_DATE             01/01/2020
END_TIME             02:00:00
DRY_STEP             00:05:00
WET_STEP             00:05:00
ROUTING_STEP         60
REPORT_STEP          00:15:00

[OUTFALLS]
O1   0   FREE

[JUNCTIONS]
;;Name Elev MaxDepth InitDepth SurDepth Aponded
J1     10   5   0   0   0
J2     5    5   0   0   0

[CONDUITS]
C1  J1  J2  400  0.013  0  0  0
C2  J2  O1  400  0.013  0  0  0

[XSECTIONS]
C1  CIRCULAR  1.5  0  0  0  1
C2  CIRCULAR  1.5  0  0  0  1

[POLLUTANTS]
;;Name Units Crain Cgw Crdii Kdecay SnowOnly CoPollut CoFrac Cdwf Cinit
P1  MG/L  0  0  0  0  NO  *  0  0  0

[DWF]
J1  FLOW  1.0
J1  P1    10

[REPORT]
NODES ALL
LINKS ALL
